    "result_text": "Full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, no failures).\n\n## Summary\n\nThe `initials` field is a computed, read-only response property, so I placed it where the other computed field (`displayName`) already lives \u2014 the response DTO schema plus the mapper \u2014 rather than on the entity or in a request-handling function.\n\n**`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added an `initials` property to the `Owner` schema (read-only), alongside `displayName`, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\n**`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added `@Mapping(target = \"initials\", expression = \"java(initials(owner))\")` and a small `initials(owner)` default method, mirroring the existing `displayName` pattern. The letter-extraction is factored into a private `initial(name)` helper (single responsibility, null/empty-safe) so `initials` just composes `initial(first) + initial(last)`, yielding e.g. `J.S.`.\n\nNo new catch-all logic \u2014 the responder (`RespondWithOwner`) already delegates to the mapper, so nothing else needed to change.",
